   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello,</div><div><br></div><div>When using stan_polr in rstanarm (version 2.14.1 Rcpp_0.12.7) in R 3.3.2, I get the following error after sampling has (apparently successfully) completed:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nlist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coefficients </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coefs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ses</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> zeta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> residuals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fitted</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">values </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> argument </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;data&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> missing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">no</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">default</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m calling stan_polr as follows:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">stan_polr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Y ~ X&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> R2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.25</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior_counts </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dirichlet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1012</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>Is there anything I can do to resolve or workaround this error?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for any advice!</div><div><br></div><div>~Nathan</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
